# Ragù alla Bolognese

The classic meat ragù of Emilia-Romagna, slow-cooked for 3-4 hours and traditionally served with tagliatelle.

## Ingredients
- Ground beef and pork
- Tomato
- Onion
- Celery
- Carrot
- Wine
- Milk (unusual but authentic)

## Technique
The ragù is slow-cooked for 3-4 hours, developing deep flavor through long braising. The milk is an authentic ingredient that helps tenderize the meat and balance acidity — it is not a cream substitute.

This dish exemplifies the Emilia-Romagna tradition and pairs best with [[tagliatelle]] due to the flat, wide shape that captures the rich meat sauce.
